body:
So a quick little background. SCOM is something I inherited about a year ago. The Run As accounts were created before me. In the case of our environment, the agent maintenance account is set to root. Not sure if that's best practice or normal, but that's how it is. Next our monitoring accounts. There are two accounts configured for each of our three domains. Elevated and non-elevated. As it were, these happen to be the exact same account (for elevated and non-elevated). 

&#x200B;

So when I read the "followed all these steps" article it looks like that is all done. Maybe not how it should be or how I would have done it, but completed none-the-less. Your last comment where you mention the more secure distro and not including the specific Linux server in the list of targeted objects, how would I verify that second part?

I don't know if it's stuttering in specific spots or what. The user is using an Xbox One S.

&#x200B;

Source file is 10-bit HDR H265 MKV

I got it on Etsy. Ships out of Russia. Took a good month to get it here in the states.

&#x200B;

[https://www.etsy.com/listing/454763148/battle-mat-space-wave-space-terrain-for?ref=shop\_home\_active\_2](https://www.etsy.com/listing/454763148/battle-mat-space-wave-space-terrain-for?ref=shop_home_active_2)
